From b8a3485a05fb5c428bdc3f0ac8db157f08f41c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <luckyljmever@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:37:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] jakku DTS: release the TCA6424 shared reset via a
 gpio-hog (fixes JP5 Wi-Fi/cameras)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two tca6424 GPIO expanders on i2c@3160000 share one active-low RESET line
(AON CC,3). Xiaomi's 4.9 gpio-pca953x pulsed it; zbwu commented the DT
reset-gpio out, so on 5.10 (mainline pca953x) the expanders stay held in reset
and NAK i2c (probe -121) — every GPIO-gated fixed regulator then defers -517
(no Wi-Fi/BT power, no camera rails). A gpio-hog driving AON CC,3 HIGH from
gpio-controller registration releases both chips before either probes, without
the shared-claim / probe-order hazard of reset-gpios on the nodes.
---
 kernel-dts/common/tegra194-p2151-0000.dtsi | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-dts/common/tegra194-p2151-0000.dtsi b/kernel-dts/common/tegra194-p2151-0000.dtsi
index ea8df64..395e908 100644
--- a/kernel-dts/common/tegra194-p2151-0000.dtsi
+++ b/kernel-dts/common/tegra194-p2151-0000.dtsi
@@ -454,3 +454,26 @@
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * 2026-07-20: release the shared active-low RESET of the two TCA6424 GPIO
+ * expanders (gpio_expand1@23 / gpio_expand2@22 on i2c@3160000). Xiaomi's 4.9
+ * gpio-pca953x carried a custom reset-gpio pulse; zbwu commented the DT
+ * reset-gpio out ("shared reset is a dangerous design"), so on 5.10 the
+ * expanders stay held in reset and NAK i2c (pca953x probe -121 EREMOTEIO) →
+ * gpio_expand2 never registers → every GPIO-gated fixed regulator
+ * (vdd_3v3_wlan_bt = Wi-Fi/BT power, camera vana/vif, gps, ...) defers -517 →
+ * no wlan0, no cameras. A gpio-hog driving the reset line HIGH (= de-asserted,
+ * active-low reset) from AON-gpio registration — before either expander probes
+ * — releases BOTH chips without the shared-claim / probe-order hazards of
+ * putting reset-gpios on the nodes. Reset pin = AON CC,3 (matches the factory
+ * JP4 DT reset-gpio <&tegra_aon_gpio 19 0>). See docs/PHASE4_BOOT_RESULTS.md.
+ */
+&tegra_aon_gpio {
+	tca6424_reset_release {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <TEGRA194_AON_GPIO(CC, 3) GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "tca6424-shared-reset";
+	};
+};
